  "result": "Fixed: shell completion no longer drops everything after a `#` in the command line. The cause was in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default, so I set `commenters = \"\"` there.\n\nI added two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `a#b` and `#tag`. The parser and shell-completion test files pass (67 tests). I didn't run the full suite, and I didn't first run the new cases against the unfixed code to confirm they fail.\n\nI also added a changelog entry in `CHANGES.md` under a new \"Version 8.5.1 (Unreleased)\" heading, because 8.5.0 is already marked released. I didn't update `docs/`, since this is a bug fix with no documented behaviour change.",
